task: intent-second-author
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-04
branch: feature/intent-second-author
worktree: ../okay-wt-author

why: Every number this module quotes was measured on a corpus written
  by one hand — mine — and the model that now SHIPS quotes 76.7% in a
  doc comment, a module page and a changelog. A consumer demonstrated
  today, for the fourth time, that such numbers overstate: their
  leave-one-out said 98.4% and three of twelve real answers written
  AFTER the corpus were stolen by the wrong class, while LOO did not
  move when they fixed it.

what I cannot do: manufacture a second author. I am the same hand.

what I can do, and this lane is: measure the GAP a second author would
  expose, without new data.
  1. Stratify held-out accuracy by how close each message is to its
     nearest training message. If the score lives in the near
     duplicates, that is the corpus scoring itself.
  2. Perturb the held-out set MECHANICALLY — lowercase, a hedge in
     front, a trailing clause, a deterministic typo, politeness
     removed — because a mechanical shift cannot be authored to
     flatter the model, and a different author differs at least this
     much.
  3. Rewrite every load-bearing number with what comes back, or
     confirm it.

files: okay-intent tests (a new JVM suite), Models.scala doc,
  docs/modules/okay-intent.md, specs/intent-classify.md, CHANGELOG
  corrections, BACKLOG.md
